{#- Release section for CHANGELOG.md, replacing cog's built-in `remote`
    template. That one emits a version heading at level 2 and commit-type
    headings at level 4, with no blank line anywhere, so every release lands
    on MD001 for the heading jump, MD022 around every heading, MD032 around
    every list, and MD012 at the splice.

    `cog bump` writes this block into CHANGELOG.md by splitting the file at
    its first `- - -` line, then writing `- - -\n`, this block, `- - -\n`, and
    the rest of the old file. The rest still starts with the newline that
    closed the old separator line, so the newest release sits directly under
    its separator while every older one sits one blank line under its own.

    A leading blank line here would therefore be right at the top of the file
    and doubled at every older boundary, and MD012 rejects the double. The
    marker below takes that first line instead: it is legal both directly
    under a thematic break and one blank line under one, and it supplies the
    blank line MD022 wants above the version heading. It renders to nothing.
    Widening the CHANGELOG.md entry in .rumdl.toml is the alternative, and it
    would blind the file to the structural breakage these rules exist for. -#}
{%- import "macros" as macros -%}
<!-- release -->

{% if version.tag and from.tag -%}
## [{{ version.tag }}]({{ repository_url ~ "/compare/" ~ from.tag ~ ".." ~ version.tag }}) - {{ date | date(format="%Y-%m-%d") }}
{% elif version.tag and from.id -%}
## [{{ version.tag }}]({{ repository_url ~ "/compare/" ~ from.id ~ ".." ~ version.tag }}) - {{ date | date(format="%Y-%m-%d") }}
{% else -%}
{% set from_shorthand = from.id | truncate(length=7, end="") -%}
{% set to_shorthand = version.id | truncate(length=7, end="") -%}
## Unreleased ([{{ from_shorthand ~ ".." ~ to_shorthand }}]({{ repository_url ~ "/compare/" ~ from_shorthand ~ ".." ~ to_shorthand }}))
{% endif -%}
{% for value in commits | group_by_type %}
### {{ value.0 | upper_first }}

{% for scope, scoped_commits in value.1 | group_by(attribute="scope") -%}
{% for commit in scoped_commits | sort(attribute="scope") -%}
{{ macros::remote(commit=commit) }}
{% endfor -%}
{% endfor -%}
{% for commit in value.1 | unscoped -%}
{{ macros::remote(commit=commit) }}
{% endfor -%}
{% endfor -%}
